# REPL command names and help texts. Only the TEXT moves to flash -- the table
# itself keeps its function pointers and stays in RAM, because ro_ptr is a
# 16-bit pgm_read_word and a function pointer on mega2560 (256K flash) is not.
cmd_help help
cmd_query ?
cmd_list list
cmd_state state
cmd_memory memory
cmd_images images
cmd_pause pause
cmd_upgrade upgrade
cmd_live live
cmd_resume resume
cmd_reset reset
cmd_clear clear
cmd_undo undo
cmd_latch latch
cmd_commit commit
cmd_settings settings
cmd_save save
cmd_load load
cmd_quit quit
cmd_exit exit
h_help Show this help
h_list List rules (F=flash E=eeprom-backed R=ram P=patches a #param S=setting)
h_state Show current values
h_memory Show code/RAM usage
h_images List the images linked into this firmware
h_upgrade Receive a CandySpeak image into a flash region (hex lines, . to end)
h_pause Stop execution (inspect/edit)
h_live Freeze rules, keep I/O (poke hardware)
h_resume Resume execution (rebuild if edited)
h_reset Reset to initial values
h_clear Drop RAM patches (keep ROM)
h_undo Take back the last typed line, or the last N
h_latch on or off, device output
h_commit Commit pending values
h_settings Show stored settings (params and pin config)
h_save Save state to storage
h_load Load state from storage
h_quit Exit interactive mode

# Storage and image names, for /memory and /images.
RAM RAM
ROM ROM
EEPROM EEPROM

# /list and /state filters and column headings.
all all
timers timers
var
variables variables
input input
output output
running running
stopped stopped
state state
instr instr
decl decl
str str
names names
hdr hdr
graph graph
objects objects
modules modules
buffers buffers
system system
struct struct
stack stack
margin margin
code code
free free

# /memory row: the device list. One list, not in+out -- direction is a runtime
# property now, so a pin cannot be filed under the direction it was declared with.
io io

# /memory row: the REPL line buffer, carved off the top of the arena
line line

# /latch argument, and the value it prints back in /state
on on
off off
